---
import { publicImage as optimizePublicArtwork } from '../lib/config';
export const prerender = true;
import Content from '../layouts/Content.astro';
import LegalStatus from '../components/LegalStatus.astro';
import EntityFaq from '../components/EntityFaq.astro';
---

<Content
  kicker="Company"
  title="About avaTOK"
  description="avaTOK is a creator platform for paid live streaming and 1:1 video sessions — creators publish paid listings, people book or join, and creators get paid."
  image="/og/about.png"
  lead="AvaTOK is a global creator platform from Ava Global International, Inc., a Delaware company founded by American and Indian founders."
  updated="2026-09-15"
>
  <h2 id="status">A US company with American and Indian founders</h2>
  <p>
    avaTOK is the platform brand of <strong>Ava Global International, Inc.</strong>, a domestic
    Delaware corporation. Our founders are American and Indian, and we are building a global
    platform where people earn money from what they already know and who they already are.
  </p>
  <LegalStatus variant="full" />

  <figure class="editorial-photo">
    <img src={optimizePublicArtwork('/genz-friends.jpg', { width: 1280, fit: 'scale-down' })} alt="Four friends laughing together over a phone" />
    <figcaption>Built so a conversation can be worth something to both people in it.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2>What we're building</h2>
  <p>
    avaTOK is a <strong>creator platform for paid live streaming and paid 1:1 video sessions</strong>.
    Plenty of people have something others will pay for — a skill, a subject they know cold, advice,
    coaching, company, an hour of real attention. What they usually lack is the boring machinery
    around it: a way to price it, a place to be found, a calendar, and a way to actually get paid.
    That machinery is the product.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>A creator publishes a listing.</strong> They choose a category, describe what they
      offer, and set their price in tokens — 1 token = ₹1. Listing is free.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>People browse and book.</strong> A viewer joins a paid live event, or books a private
      1:1 video session in a slot the creator has opened on their calendar.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The session happens on avaTOK.</strong> Live streams and 1:1 sessions both run inside
      the platform, so nobody has to swap phone numbers or move to another app.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The creator gets paid.</strong> Earnings land in their avaTOK wallet and can be
      withdrawn to a verified payout method. See <a href="/payouts">Payouts &amp; Withdrawals</a>.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Categories, not one narrow niche</h2>
  <p>
    Creators list across a range of categories — teaching and tutoring, coaching and advice,
    consultations, performance and entertainment, wellness and conversation. What they have in
    common is that the thing being sold is <em>time and attention</em>, live, from one person to
    another. Browse what is live now on the <a href="/marketplace">marketplace</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Messaging, a masked avaTOK number that keeps a creator's real phone number private, and AI
    tooling exist to support that — they are how a booking gets arranged safely, not the product
    itself.
  </p>
  <div class="note">
    A note on AI: our products use artificial intelligence, and AI can make mistakes. We share more
    in our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>. We've also made our best efforts to use
    AI-generated imagery responsibly — if you ever find something objectionable, email
    <a href="mailto:support@avatok.ai">support@avatok.ai</a> and we'll remove it. It was never
    intentional.
  </p>

  <h2>What we value</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Creators get paid.</strong> The price is set by the creator, shown before anyone
      commits, and the earnings are theirs minus a stated platform fee. No surprises in either
      direction — see <a href="/pricing-fees">Pricing &amp; Fees</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Privacy by default.</strong> A creator publishes a listing, not a phone number. Your
      real number stays masked behind an avaTOK number.</li>
    <li><strong>Say what is true.</strong> We are early, payments may be limited during rollout,
      and we say so clearly rather than burying it.</li>
    <li><strong>Built responsibly.</strong> Consent for recording, safety rules that apply to both
      sides of a session, and honest AI are part of the product, not an afterthought.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>American and Indian founders, built for the world</h2>
  <p>
    avaTOK is made with care by American and Indian founders for creators and audiences around the
    world. Want to help build it? See our
    <a href="/careers">open roles</a>. If you are an investor who wants to back an early global
    creator platform, we would like to hear from you —
    <a href="mailto:hello@avatok.ai">hello@avatok.ai</a>.
  </p>

  {/* [WEB-SEO-6] Entity definition + FAQPage — see the component header. */}
  <EntityFaq />

  <h2 id="press">Press & media</h2>
  <p>
    For press, partnership, or media inquiries, reach us at
    <a href="mailto:support@avatok.ai">support@avatok.ai</a> and we'll get back to you. You can also
    read the latest from our team on the <a href="/blog">avaTOK blog</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>
    Questions, ideas, or feedback? We'd love to hear from you — visit our
    <a href="/contact">contact page</a> or email <a href="mailto:support@avatok.ai">support@avatok.ai</a>.
  </p>
</Content>
